{"aggregate_id": "01M7X6B1MARTS68ADD3VQJD0Y6", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01M7X6B3AZTZC2AMXMJA8C3MC0", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"actor": "noreply@anthropic.com", "created_at": "2026-11-20T19:18:41.008601+00:00", "friendly_name": "Host-aware mode predicate for tool-surface planners", "mission_id": "01M7X6B1MARTS68ADD3VQJD0Y6", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "host-aware-mode-predicate-01M7X6B1", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "On Windows the file system reports fixed modes, so planners that compare the observed mode with a planned POSIX mode plan a chmod that never takes effect: the startup skill sync and upgrade --dry-run report the same phantom repairs forever, while doctor says the project is clean. This Mission makes one host-aware mode comparison the only way planners decide mode equality and adds an architectural gate that keeps it that way (#4927, #4810).", "purpose_tldr": "A converged Windows project stops re-planning file-mode repairs it can never apply, on every CLI start and every upgrade preview.", "target_branch": "issue-4927-host-aware-mode-predicate", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-11-20T19:18:41.759229+00:00"}
